ankly  despite their propaganda pushing out  small businesses preventing them from  being able to have success and the like  well i think we are seeing a great  divergence i mean you have in my  district  a market cap of 10 trillion dollars  and a lot of small businesses a lot of  left behind communities  aren't participating in modern wealth  generation and then i thought gabe wrote  a very  inspiring piece where workers have  basically become  accessories to robots i'm all for  technological advance that's going to  lead to productivity where that's going  to  help benefit the american people but we  should not use  technology as a tool to grab power  away from workers to management and  dehumanize the workplace  and we need regulations that would  prevent  companies from doing that well one of  the things that i think you experienced  gabe  was basically just the the atomization  effect of  working at amazon that i think it often  escapes the debate  there are negative consequences for that  in terms of and  just an ability to relate to each other  and as  human beings within a workplace aren't  there  yeah ben i think people you know they  they like to be with one another i think  you know the workplace there's no secret  that a job the point of a job is  certainly to get paid but i think there  are other aspects of a job such as  you know building a community within an  area and really  building those relationships with your  supervisor with your fellow colleagues  and certainly places you know with this  big business they come into these  communities  and they sort of just break up and don't  allow people  in these areas to really uh build those  relationships with people  uh you know in those areas congressman  quickly i  i feel like one of the other elements of  this that we have to appreciate  is that there doesn't seem to be one  easy answer on this  people want the convenience of amazon  they want the ability to have things  show up within a day or two  a